					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-03 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/187/482261382_ae903d9462_m.jpg" alt="" width="240" height="160" /><br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/194/482271073_9e9cb20cc5_m.jpg" alt="" width="240" height="160" /><br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/173/482261602_b746975f8a_m.jpg" alt="" width="240" height="160" /><br /><em><br />Blue Scholars perform for the Seattle May Day Rally, May 1, 2007 at the Seattle Center. Photos by Daps1</em><br /><br />Yo Massliners and those viewing from all over the world: Did you know that Massline has their own Flickr site? If anyone wants to hook us up with a Pro account, holler!<br /><br />http://www.flickr.com/photos/masslinemedia/<br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-02 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://i14.tinypic.com/4kwfgxu.jpg" alt="" width="390" height="214" /><br /><br /><br /><br /><img src="http://i18.tinypic.com/4r9r5ec.jpg" alt="" width="430" /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-01 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>NO HUMAN IS ILLEGAL!&nbsp;&nbsp; that&#39;s the message resonating loud and clear throughout american communities today - a message that must be delivered to congress for immediate action.&nbsp;&nbsp; organizers are asking that supporters of immigration reform rock white tees in a show of solidarity -- size and length are entirely up to you.&nbsp;&nbsp; there is a march planned this afternoon from 2-4pm begining at westlake,&nbsp; so hawk those mariner&#39;s tickets and stand alongside your true compatriots.&nbsp;&nbsp; happy may day, fam...<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-29 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><strong>Sa-I-Gu aka The LA Uprising</strong><br /><br />Damn, has it really been 15 years? On <strong>April 29, 1992</strong> the City of Los Angeles erupted into a full-blown rebellion. I remember the images on the television screen vividly. I remember moms and pops waiting on phone updates from fam in LA. What I remember most, however, was the feeling that something aint right in this country which I was taught to revere and love. Now that I look back, this is probably where I really started connecting politics with hip-hop music and the feeling that things aint right. <br /><p>I remember Kam&#39;s &quot;Peace Treaty&quot; and Ice Cube spitting &quot;April 29 was power to the people...&quot; on The Predator album. I remember the media whipping up the gang hysteria. There was a big gap between how the &quot;gang problem&quot; was portrayed in the media and how emcees were portraying it in rhyme. I remember more and more of my friends joining gangs in and around &#39;92. I was twelve years old.</p><p>I&#39;m 27 now, and I&#39;m hours away from rocking a stage at a block party (see 4/27 blog entry) in the heart of LA on the anniversary of the uprising. The music I make now owes alot of it&#39;s inspiration to April 29, 1992. It&#39;s a new generation of folks. Same struggle. Still standing. </p><p>Peace to <strong>Bambu</strong> on this historic day. Congrats on the new album homie!</p><p>Get your history lesson on: <a href="http://www.geocities.com/aufheben2/auf_1_la.html">The Rebellion in Los Angeles</a></p><p>Peace,<br />Geo</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-28 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>Respect to the Massive Monkees crew celebrating their 8-year
anniversary this weekend. Today is the super-official mayor-certified
Massive Monkee Day and the sun is out in the 206. What else can you ask
for?<br />
<strong><br />
Saturday<br />
April, 28 2007<br />
MASSIVE MONKEES 8 YEAR ANNIVERSARY </strong><br />
University of Washington HUB North Den<br />
4pm - 10pm<br />
All-Ages | Cost: $10<br />
w/ djblesOne vs. Bruce Illest<br />
1 on 1 footwork &amp; crew battles<br />
<br />
featuring special guests: <br />
Remind - Style Elements CA <br />
